# Every text file is checked out with LF, on Windows too. Tests compare checked-in text with what
# Beacon generates or writes, which is LF: golden files, the .kql pack, FIELDS.md, the lens SPEC
# copies, generated references. Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf turned them into CRLF on
# checkout, and each such test had to learn to undo it. Binary files are detected and left alone;
# fxsession's recorded sessions opt out of conversion entirely (their own .gitattributes).
* text=auto eol=lf
